canonical_claim.statement:
[Corrected display, from the validator] "$\lim_{n\to\infty}\Pr(|n\widehat V_2^*(A^{\mathcal O};Z) - n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta)| > \epsilon) = 0$" (the print has $< \epsilon$).
[Statement with its hypotheses] Under Assumptions 2 and 3, with $X_i = \theta_iY_i$, common variance $\sigma_n^2 = \mathrm{var}(X_i) > 0$, pairwise correlations $\rho_{ij} = \mathrm{cov}(X_i, X_j)/\sigma_n^2$ (P011-T21) and $\widehat V_2^*(A^{\mathcal O};Z) = \frac{\hat\sigma_\theta^2}{n}\left[1 + \frac1n\sum_{i \in \mathcal V_S}\sum_{j \in \mathcal V_S}A^{\mathcal O}_{ij}\rho_{ij}\right]$:
(i) [exact] $n\widehat V_2^*(A^{\mathcal O};Z) - n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) = k_n\left(\hat\sigma_\theta^2 - \sigma_n^2\right)$, where $k_n = 1 + \frac1n\sum_i\sum_j A^{\mathcal O}_{ij}\rho_{ij} = n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta)/\sigma_n^2$;
(ii) $\hat\sigma_\theta^2 - \sigma_n^2 - M_n \to 0$ in probability, where $M_n = \frac1n\sum_i(\mathrm{E}[X_i] - \beta)^2$ (P011-T12 (i));
(iii) hence the corrected display holds, for every $\epsilon > 0$, if $M_n \to 0$, in particular if $\mathrm{E}[\theta_iY_i] = \beta$ for every $i$; correcting the inequality sign alone does not make it hold under Assumptions 2 and 3 only (P011-T11, where $M_n \to 1$).

[Corrected text, from the validator] Define $X_i = \theta_iY_i$, $\sigma_\theta^2 = \mathrm{var}(X_i)$ (the common variance of Assumption 3), and $\rho_{ij} = \mathrm{cov}(X_i, X_j)/\sigma_\theta^2$ when $\sigma_\theta^2 > 0$ ($\rho_{ij} = 0$ by convention if $\sigma_\theta^2 = 0$); replace all four occurrences of $\rho_i$ in the proof by $\rho_{ij}$. The auxiliary estimator is $\widehat V_2^*(A^{\mathcal O};Z) = \frac{\hat\sigma_\theta^2}{n}\left[1 + \frac1n\sum_{i \in \mathcal V_S}\sum_{j \in \mathcal V_S}A^{\mathcal O}_{ij}\rho_{ij}\right]$, and "all $\rho_{ij} \le 1$".
[Formal content] Under Assumption 3 for $i, j \in \mathcal V_S$ and Definition 1:
(i) $n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) = \sigma_\theta^2\left[1 + \frac1n\sum_{i \in \mathcal V_S}\sum_{j \in \mathcal V_S}A^{\mathcal O}_{ij}\rho_{ij}\right]$;
(ii) $\rho_{ij} \le 1$ for all $i, j$, and therefore $\widehat V_2^*(A^{\mathcal O};Z) \le \widehat V_2(A^{\mathcal O};Z)$ in every realization;
(iii) [an instance showing that a single index cannot carry the correlations] on the path $1 - 2 - 3$ with $U, V$ independent, $\Pr(\cdot = 1) = \Pr(\cdot = -1) = 1/2$, and $X = (U, \tfrac35U + \tfrac45V, V)$: all three variances are 1, $\rho_{12} = 3/5$, $\rho_{23} = 4/5$, $\rho_{13} = 0$, and both sides of (i) equal $29/15$ ($n = 3$).

[Corrected text, from the validator] "Define $\hat v_{ij} = (\theta_iY_i - \hat\beta)(\theta_jY_j - \hat\beta)$, and let $a_{ij} = 1$ if edge $\{i,j\}$ is selected in the candidate graph, and 0 otherwise, for $i < j$."
[Formal content] Let $a = (a_{ij})_{1 \le i < j \le n} \in \{0, 1\}^{n(n-1)/2}$ and let $A$ be the $n \times n$ matrix with $A_{ij} = A_{ji} = a_{ij}$ for $i < j$ and $A_{ii} = 0$. The map $a \mapsto A$ is a bijection onto the binary symmetric zero-diagonal matrices, and under it:
(i) $(\Theta Y - \hat\beta 1)^{\mathsf T}A(\Theta Y - \hat\beta 1) = 2\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=i+1}^{n}\hat v_{ij}a_{ij}$;
(ii) $(A1)_i = \sum_{j=1}^{i-1}a_{ji} + \sum_{j=i+1}^{n}a_{ij}$ for every $i$, so $A1 \preceq d$ (element-wise $\le$) is the degree constraint of (3.6);
(iii) $A \succeq A_R$ if and only if $a_{ij} = 1$ for every $\{i,j\} \in \mathcal E_R$ with $i < j$;
(iv) hence $A$ is optimal for (3.5) if and only if $a$ is optimal for (3.6) with the variables of the edges in $\mathcal E_R$ fixed at one; the optimal values differ by the factor 2; and $n^2\widehat V_1(A^m;Z) = n\hat\sigma_\theta^2 + 2w^\ast$ with $w^\ast$ the optimal value of (3.6);
(v) with $\hat v_{ij} = 1$ for all $i < j$, $1^{\mathsf T}A1 = 2\sum_{i<j}a_{ij}$ and (3.6) is (3.8).

[Corrected claim, from the validator] Appendix B says that the package has "depvar for calculating the variance estimates (3.1) and (3.7)". As staged, the three helpers of depvar use R's var(x), whose divisor is $n - 1$, where the paper defines $\hat\sigma_\theta^2$ with divisor $n$. Fix $n > 1$, $x_i = \theta_iY_i$, $\bar x = \hat\beta$, $z_i = x_i - \bar x$, $S = \sum_iz_i^2$, an adjacency matrix $A$, $C_A = \sum_{i,j}A_{ij}z_iz_j$, $D_A = \sum_{i,j}A_{ij}$ and $D' = \sum_i\min\{d_i, n-1\}$. The printed formulas are $\widehat V_1(A;Z) = \frac{S}{n^2} + \frac{C_A}{n^2}$, $\widehat V_2(A;Z) = \frac{S}{n^2}\left(1 + \frac{D_A}{n}\right)$, $\widehat V_2'(Z) = \frac{S}{n^2}\left(1 + \frac{D'}{n}\right)$; the staged helpers compute $V_1^{R} = \frac{S}{n(n-1)} + \frac{C_A}{n^2}$, $V_2^{R} = \frac{S}{n(n-1)}\left(1 + \frac{D_A}{n}\right)$, $V_2'^{R} = \frac{S}{n(n-1)}\left(1 + \frac{D'}{n}\right)$. Then:
(i) $V_1^{R} - \widehat V_1(A;Z) = \frac{S}{n^2(n-1)} = \frac{\hat\sigma_\theta^2}{n(n-1)}$ (only the first term of (3.1) is rescaled);
(ii) $V_2^{R} = \frac{n}{n-1}\widehat V_2(A;Z)$ and $V_2'^{R} = \frac{n}{n-1}\widehat V_2'(Z)$;
(iii) each code value is at least the printed one, strictly when $S > 0$; and for fixed data a matrix maximizes $V_1^{R}$ (respectively $V_2^{R}$) over $\mathcal A(Z)$ if and only if it maximizes $\widehat V_1$ (respectively $\widehat V_2$);
(iv) if $|x_i - \beta| \le c_1$ for all $i$, then $0 \le n\left(V_1^{R} - \widehat V_1(A;Z)\right) \le \frac{4c_1^2}{n-1}$ for every $A$;
(v) with var(x) replaced by mean((x - mean(x))^2), i.e. by $S/n$, the three helpers equal (3.1), (3.7) and (3.9).
